// cell.nv — the value a row holds, and the bytes it becomes.
//
// A row is a `[Cell]`, and a cell is one of five things SQLite's
// storage classes name: an integer, a float, text, a blob, or NULL.
// Nothing else appears in a page, so nothing else appears here.
//
// WHY THIS TYPE LIVES IN btree-nv AND NOT IN sql-engine-nv
//
// novodb carries two of it.  `parse.Value` is what a literal in the
// SQL text becomes (`VInt`, `VFloat`, `VStr`, `VNull`, `VBlob`) and
// `btree.Cell` is what a row in the tree holds (`CInt`, `CFloat`,
// `CStr`, `CNull`, `CBlob`) — the same five classes, twice, with
// `parse.value_to_cell` copying between them at every INSERT.  The
// duplication is free inside one package and is not free across two:
// it would put the bridge function on the package boundary, where a
// consumer would have to know both spellings and which side of the
// call it was on.  So there is one type, it is the STORAGE one, and
// sql-engine-nv's literals produce it directly.
//
// The encoding below is `page_btree.nv`'s, unchanged: a one-byte tag
// then the payload, big-endian throughout.  The float case is the one
// that is not settled — novodb encodes a float as the TEXT of
// `string_of_float` because the stdlib had no `float.to_bits` when it
// was written, which is neither compact nor round-trip exact.  This
// package declares the bit form and the README says so.

// A stored value: one of the five classes a page can hold.
//
// Byte tags, as they appear in an encoded row — the numbers are the
// format, not an implementation detail, so they are written here
// rather than derived:
//
// | tag | variant  | payload |
// | --- | --- | --- |
// | 0 | `CNull` | none |
// | 1 | `CInt` | 8 bytes, big-endian two's complement |
// | 2 | `CFloat` | 8 bytes, IEEE-754 binary64, big-endian |
// | 3 | `CStr` | 4-byte big-endian length, then that many UTF-8 bytes |
// | 4 | `CBlob` | 4-byte big-endian length, then that many raw bytes |
pub enum Cell
    CNull
    CInt(n: Int)
    CFloat(f: Float)
    CStr(s: Str)
    CBlob(bytes: [Int])

// A cell holding an integer.
//
// ```novo
// use cell
//
// let c = cell.of_int(42)
// ```
pub fn of_int(n: Int) -> Cell
    todo("btree-nv.cell.of_int")

